// Strokeline Education Style 9: Mind Map Brainstorm
// Purpose: Copy-ready template. One hub idea, four colored branches, short answer leaves.
// Demo topic: Photosynthesis (same topic as the Chalkboard style, so the styles compare side by side).
// Look: warm desk background, white paper sheet with soft shadow, yellow hub with a leaf icon,
//   one color per branch (deep branch pill + pale leaf pills), an icon on every node,
//   sticky-note tips, and a recap with Key Takeaway / Memory Trick / Common Mistake cards.
// Scenes: 1 title, 2 branches, 3 full map, 4 recap.
//
// HOW TO REUSE
//  1. Replace "Photosynthesis" (scenes 1, 2, 3) with your topic.
//  2. Rename the 4 branch pills (keep them to one short word, about 8 characters max).
//  3. Edit leaf text (about 15 characters max at SIZE 42) and swap leaf icons (NAME ...).
//  4. Scene 3 shows exactly 12 text objects, the validator limit (W_TOO_CROWDED).
//     To add a leaf, remove another one, or split the map across two scenes.
//  5. Each branch uses 3 colors: deep fill (white text), pale tint (leaf), dark text (leaf).
//  6. Some Lucide icons (sun, candy, sparkles, triangle-alert) draw messily in the hand-drawn
//     style. Safe picks: leaf, star, droplet, zap, refresh-cw, apple, wind, map-pin, eraser.
//
// Validator status: run with the Strokeline app validator (web/scripts/validate.mjs).
VERSION 1.0
CANVAS 1920 1080
BACKGROUND #FBE9C6
STYLE handdrawn
FONT handwritten
STROKE 4

SCENE 1 "One big idea"
  SAY "Before cramming facts, drop one anchor on the page and let everything else grow from it."
    DURATION 5s
    TONE hook
  CREATE paper AS RECTANGLE
    POSITION 960 540
    WIDTH 1840
    HEIGHT 1000
    CORNERS 40
    FILL #FFFDF8
